{"title":"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/5415091b808a487eb76393a850ebb0107375c144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1 = \\{2,0,3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aea06e1d22e8430a3065673c7658d5482aca143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2 = \\{2,20,202,2023\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" /> Find the last digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc983b7c154bda86c6cf190042b393211940b15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{a\\in S_1,b\\in S_2}a^b.\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be independently chosen vertices lying in the square with coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d571752d0ced6b142e2aaa7b980f359e56e34e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/149f6a15ba033bfb273e7af037a90ffe9dbaa218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f3bf596b5b5551059a9d28fbbcc0cd576d4838.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, -1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The probability that the centroid of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> lies in the first quadrant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> for relatively prime positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pigs like to eat carrots. Suppose a pig randomly chooses 6 letters from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c5f3cf78311bad1e1d16fcc513427f0e0e61103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{c,a,r,o,t\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> Then, the pig randomly arranges the 6 letters to form a \"word\". If the 6 letters don't spell carrot, the pig gets frustrated and tries to spell it again (by rechoosing the 6 letters and respelling them). What is the expected number of tries it takes for the pig to spell \"carrot\"?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef36d8b3c71cd00802eb6c16c99f2b131d5e28f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_1 = F_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2ba1b96c5a8886d1b566ea7560181e22e43f73ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_n = F_{n-1} + F_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47affecc93688552c8eca8bc13560d52b4cc28a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> be the Fibonacci numbers. If distinct positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a874baf27c19c605e774298d3e38a4dddc2d318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0787e8d78aa455ee6c77441674ff7e39f65d62f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{a_1}+F_{a_2}+\\dots+F_{a_n}=2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"19\" />, find the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8981aaf16e66c7ded7482dbfce5d9036aeb02bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\dots+a_n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> of dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec91cfa0bd7ca6e6803dce5b6e9ab2a1c7acb198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\times 8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is choosen such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01ba24a78a0b15cd0d287e9e6a1d133a40c4e18f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{APD}+\\angle{BPC} = 180^{\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"201\" height=\"16\" /> Find the sum of the maximum, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and minimum values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17bb86c67c87823f813bacd32c6ec84b18047f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(PA)(PC)+(PB)(PD).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" /> If you think there is no maximum, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e45cf28c5a2083fe1ec2830ab30da1fea6d8ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest odd prime that does not divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b54f2362019eb1a6d17fb54480f3a1db1551bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{75!} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At FenZhu High School, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th graders have a 60\\% of chance of having a dog and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th graders have a 40\\% chance of having a dog. Suppose there is a classroom of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th grader and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th graders. If exactly one person owns a dog, then the probability that a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th grader owns the dog is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888fed89e19182447f85b3cb6676548a49395284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"34\" /> for relatively prime positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> has chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5dfe79f87b08489fe323e03ccfc95fd8126f9d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> lie on two different sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecee609050b0744995a1b79ec0fcd162a97441b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> Both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> are tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> If the sum of the maximum and minimum values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21a4cf89248ee36f4b11ed6439745dbd9f86ee9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888fed89e19182447f85b3cb6676548a49395284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"34\" /> find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of the maximum and minimum values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5fd196e16e2ae11d699eae59cf21712ba384ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8x^2+7xy+5y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> under the constraint that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9c6054844c24388a0272fa74b2cb9c986f2efa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2+5xy+3y^2 = 88.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2023 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsect